*********************************************************************************************************************************************************
							This set of scripts is for polishing weapon animations
							It is especially relevant for game animators.
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************
									Parent In
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************
	what is he doing?

				recalculates animation of objects to external locator
				this is one of the most used scripts - not only in weapon animation but also in many other places
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	how it work
				if select one object:
				bakes the animation of the selected object to external locator
				if select two or more object:
				recalculates the animation of objects to the locator system, 
				where all locators are inside the locator of the last selected object
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	usage
				if select sword only:
				you can animate the hand, and the sword will be independent of it
				if you choose a hand and a sword: 
				then you can correct the position of the hand relative to the sword
				if select both Hands controls, and select sword Control: 
				hands will move inside the sword (it will be easy to make a grip with two hands)
				And so on and so forth
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************
									Make Aim
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************
	what is he doing?

				allows you to adjust the trajectory of the weapon (or any object) tip
				this is one of the most used scripts - not only in weapon animation but also in many other places
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	how it work

				bakes the rotation of the selected object (weapon or wrist or anything else) 
				by 2 locators, one of which controls the TOP of rotation, and the second SIDE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	usage
	
				After launch, 2 locators will appear, the first highlighted - TOP - immediately pull it to the top of the weapon. 
				After that, either with the button in the menu - or with the standard hotkey - arrow to the right 
				- select SIDE and pull it in the perpendicular direction - towards the blade.
				And when everything is ready, click on an empty spot in the scene. The script is recalculated
				
